-- Function — a FenelFunction. Pure callable spec, optionally with
-- triggers (function_triggers) for durable execution and instances
-- (function_instances) for runtime state.
--
-- Static rows: none. Identity + the per-field label/widget hint are lifted
-- from the directives below (FM-retire-E1 Step 2 + Step 5); the auto-register
-- loop in system-entities.ts registers the entity. The pre-flip
-- `defineSystemEntity` is GONE.
--
-- The `function` field name doubles as a TS keyword, but Fenel's parser admits
-- it at field position via `isFieldNameToken` (admits keywords with trailing
-- `:`). No grammar work owed.
--   - `@fieldLabel "function" "Spec"` — so the field label doesn't duplicate
--     the entity label.
--   - `@widget "function" "function-editor"` + `@helpText` — the editor mounts
--     the FunctionSpecBuilder for this field.
--
-- The pre-flip `fieldDefaults` (active → true, version → 1) are DROPPED as
-- runtime-dead (FM-retire-E1 Step 5, Scope A): the `functions` table owns those
-- as column defaults (`active BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE`, `version INTEGER DEFAULT
-- 1`, migration 0024) and `upsertFunction` INSERTs without them; there is no
-- generic AdminForm create path for `function` (no ENTITY_CONFIG entry). The
-- field-level annotations merely duplicated the DB defaults — the textbook
-- FieldDef.default anti-pattern. No `@default` directive (guardrail).
--
-- TODO: the `function` field's `{}` (empty record) shape is preserved
-- bug-compatibly from the pre-3d TS literal. The real schema for a
-- FenelFunction spec (params, returns, body, requires) is out of
-- scope for this phase; lands when the function entity gets a fully-
-- typed shape.

@entity
@codeName "function"
@label "Function"
@description "A FenelFunction — pure callable spec, optionally with triggers (function_triggers) for durable execution and instances (function_instances) for runtime state."
@icon "route"
@fieldLabel "function" "Spec"
@widget "function" "function-editor"
@helpText "function" "FenelFunction spec — params, returns, body"
Function = Function name: String active: Boolean function: {} version: Number
